# Makefile.mutos -- kernel_opt: assembles every real kernel *.s here with
# the REAL "as", twice, to gather real-hardware ground truth for
# STATUS.md's open item 6 (the "-L" question):
#
#   noL   ->  "<name>.o"   assembled WITHOUT "-L" (as.1's documented
#             default, which excludes compiler-internal "L"-prefixed
#             labels from the symbol table).
#   L     ->  "<name>.oL"  assembled WITH "-L" explicitly (labels
#             included).
#
# Every already-committed "<name>.o.golden" in this directory carries
# L-number labels, which the documented default should exclude -- see
# CLAUDE.md's "Known, deliberate exception" for mutos_as's own "-L".
# Whether the original kernel build actually invoked "as -L" is not
# known. After copying "noL"'s and "L"'s outputs back to the modern
# host (see ../mk_goldenbase64.sh / the sibling Linux Makefile), diff
# each fresh "<name>.o"/"<name>.oL" against the existing
# "<name>.o.golden": whichever variant matches settles the question for
# every file at once (see STATUS.md's open item 6 and
# tests/mutos_as/libc_recon/README.md, which is blocked on this same
# answer for compiled-C libc.a objects).
#
# Run from INSIDE this directory, ON THE REAL MUTOS 1700 hardware /
# emulator:
#
#   make -f Makefile.mutos noL
#   make -f Makefile.mutos L
#   make -f Makefile.mutos clean
#
# (Deliberately no "all" combining both in one invocation -- matches
# this project's established "tackle one variant/category at a time"
# practice, see tests/mutos_cc/README.md.)
#
# Uses a genuine V7/MUTOS make(1) two-suffix rule per variant
# (".s.o:" / ".s.oL:", both confirmed supported -- see
# tests/mutos_cc/Makefile.mutos's own header) instead of one explicit
# target per file. This keeps the file's total size tiny regardless of
# how many "*.s" files exist: only two recipe blocks are ever
# registered, so this sidesteps the "Make: out of memory" failure
# tests/mutos_cc's original all-62-files-explicit Makefile.mutos hit on
# real hardware (see docs/DEVLOG.md's Milestone 4 host-tooling
# findings) -- that failure came from ~124 explicit per-file recipe
# blocks exhausting a fixed-size internal table, not from a long
# dependency list by itself. "noL:"/"L:" below are plain (recipe-less)
# grouping targets, so they only ever add one long prerequisite line
# each, not new rules.
#
# NOT yet run on real MUTOS 1700 hardware -- this file's own
# reliability (in particular, whether the suffix-rule approach really
# does avoid the internal-table limit above at 61 files) is therefore
# UNVERIFIED. If it still hits a real-hardware resource limit, fall
# back to tests/mutos_cc's proven workaround: split "noL"/"L" into a
# chain of small sub-targets (see docs/DEVLOG.md's finding #2/#3 for
# that exact pattern).
#
# CONCLUDED 2026-09-28 without ever running "noL"/"L" here: the "-L"
# question this file exists to help answer was already settled by the
# first "-L" invocation tried on real hardware, "as -L -o v30ide.oL
# v30ide.s" -> "Unknown option L ignored" -- the real "as" does not
# implement "-L" at all (see ../README.md's "Result" and STATUS.md's
# open item 6). Since the flag is silently ignored rather than merely
# defaulted, "noL" and "L" are necessarily byte-identical for every
# file here, so running either adds nothing. Left unrun and unmodified
# as working infrastructure -- its own reliability at 61 files (the
# question this comment block above was written to flag) remains
# genuinely untested, but is now moot for the "-L" question itself.
#
# EXCEPTION -- mch_insw_outsw.s is deliberately left OUT of both lists
# below: its stem is already 14 characters, so even its plain ".s"
# name (16 characters) already exceeds the real MUTOS 1700 DIRSIZ=14
# filename limit (see CLAUDE.md's "Identifier length limits") -- a
# pre-existing fact about this file, not introduced by this Makefile.
# Assemble it by hand under a short on-device alias and rename the
# *.o/*.oL result back to "mch_insw_outsw.o"/"mch_insw_outsw.oL" only
# after copying it back to the modern host (where the 14-character
# limit no longer applies) -- see README.md's "mch_insw_outsw.s" section
# for the exact commands. Do not "mv" it back to the long name while
# still on MUTOS 1700 -- that would silently truncate or fail under
# DIRSIZ.
#
# Every recipe is one shell line, per make(1)'s own note (see
# tests/mutos_cc/00_smoke/Makefile.mutos) that shell state doesn't
# carry across separate recipe lines.

AS = as

.SUFFIXES: .s .o .oL

.s.o:
	$(AS) -o $*.o $*.s

.s.oL:
	$(AS) -L -o $*.oL $*.s

noL: acct.o alloc.o amx.o bio.o bus.o c.o c5170.o camx.o casp.o \
	ccons.o clocal.o clock.o clp.o cons_NOBIOS.o cram.o debug.o \
	delay.o dlock.o dosent.o dsort.o fio.o gcpc.o genio.o ifsp.o \
	ifss.o iget.o intr.o k5170.o kdebug.o load86.o lp_AC.o \
	machdep.o main.o malloc.o mch.o mem.o msdos.o nami.o \
	physio.o pipe.o prf.o prim.o ramfl.o rdwri.o sbreak.o sig.o \
	slp.o subr.o symtab.o sys.o sys1.o sys2.o sys3.o sys4.o \
	sysent.o sysx.o text.o trap.o tty.o v24.o v30ide.o

L: acct.oL alloc.oL amx.oL bio.oL bus.oL c.oL c5170.oL camx.oL \
	casp.oL ccons.oL clocal.oL clock.oL clp.oL cons_NOBIOS.oL \
	cram.oL debug.oL delay.oL dlock.oL dosent.oL dsort.oL fio.oL \
	gcpc.oL genio.oL ifsp.oL ifss.oL iget.oL intr.oL k5170.oL \
	kdebug.oL load86.oL lp_AC.oL machdep.oL main.oL malloc.oL \
	mch.oL mem.oL msdos.oL nami.oL physio.oL pipe.oL prf.oL \
	prim.oL ramfl.oL rdwri.oL sbreak.oL sig.oL slp.oL subr.oL \
	symtab.oL sys.oL sys1.oL sys2.oL sys3.oL sys4.oL sysent.oL \
	sysx.oL text.oL trap.oL tty.oL v24.oL v30ide.oL

clean:
	rm -f *.o *.oL
